From: YOUR NAME <your@email>
Subject: [PATCH] ext4: wait for tail page commit before truncating a failed write

In data=journal mode a failed buffered write can leave the folio that
straddles i_size with buffers attached to the committing transaction.
jbd2_journal_invalidate_folio() then returns -EBUSY for the partial
invalidation, which ext4_journalled_invalidate_folio() reports as:

  WARNING: fs/ext4/inode.c:3561 at ext4_journalled_invalidate_folio

ext4_truncate_down() already waits for the tail page commit before
invalidating the page cache, but the failed-write paths do not.

shuo chen's patch handled ext4_journalled_write_end(); the error path in
ext4_write_begin() can hit the same warning and is still unfixed, as
pointed out by the review of that patch.  Wait for the commit in both
paths, and keep the helper local to inode.c.

Suggested-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
Signed-off-by: shuo chen <1289151713@qq.com>
Reported-by: Farhad Alemi <farhad.alemi@berkeley.edu>
